WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.950 --> 00:00:04.770
I'm Jenna Fisher.
我是珍娜·费舍尔。

2
00:00:04.970 --> 00:00:06.070
And I'm Angela Kinsey.
我是安吉拉·金赛。

3
00:00:06.210 --> 00:00:07.370
We were on The Office together.
我们曾一起出演《办公室》。

4
00:00:07.590 --> 00:00:08.610
And we're best friends.
我们是最好的朋友。

5
00:00:08.730 --> 00:00:12.430
And now we're doing the Ultimate Office Rewatch podcast just for you.
现在我们正为你们制作《办公室》终极重温播客。

6
00:00:12.610 --> 00:00:19.410
Each week, we will break down an episode of The Office and give exclusive behind-the-scenes stories that only two people who were there can tell you.
每周，我们都会剖析一集《办公室》，并分享只有身临其境的我们两人才能告诉你的独家幕后故事。

7
00:00:19.570 --> 00:00:20.550
We're The Office ladies.
我们是“办公室女士”。

8
00:00:23.390 --> 00:00:25.010
It's party time, everybody.
派对时间到了，各位。

9
00:00:25.390 --> 00:00:26.890
It's a launch party.
这是个发布派对。

10
00:00:27.130 --> 00:00:28.670
Or is it a lunch party?
还是说是个午餐派对？

11
00:00:29.050 --> 00:00:30.030
How dare you?
你怎么敢这么说？

12
00:00:30.210 --> 00:00:31.430
Is it a lunch party?
这是个午餐派对吗？

13
00:00:32.450 --> 00:00:33.370
Get out.
出去。

14
00:00:34.090 --> 00:00:36.350
You and Kevin can get out.
你和凯文都可以出去。

15
00:00:36.870 --> 00:00:38.850
That is one of my favorite jokes.
那是我最喜欢的笑话之一。

16
00:00:39.170 --> 00:00:39.830
Lunch party.
午餐派对。

17
00:00:40.350 --> 00:00:40.830
Yeah.
是啊。

18
00:00:41.010 --> 00:00:42.130
Would that be better, Kevin?
那样会更好吗，凯文？

19
00:00:42.370 --> 00:00:44.670
Would that be better for it to say, lunch party?
写成“午餐派对”会更好吗？

20
00:00:45.930 --> 00:00:48.090
Well, it is a launch party.
好吧，这确实是个发布派对。

21
00:00:48.310 --> 00:00:50.470
It is another one-hour episode.
这又是长达一小时的一集。

22
00:00:50.490 --> 00:00:52.090
So you know what that means.
所以你知道这意味着什么。

23
00:00:52.290 --> 00:00:54.730
We're doing launch party part one today.
我们今天要做的是《发布派对》第一部分。

24
00:00:55.050 --> 00:01:02.490
This was season four, episode five, written by Jen Salata and directed by Ken Whittingham.
这是第四季第五集，由简·萨拉塔编剧，肯·惠廷汉执导。

25
00:01:03.370 --> 00:01:05.490
I mean, one of our favorite duos.
我是说，这是我们最喜欢的搭档之一。

26
00:01:05.870 --> 00:01:06.530
Oh, yeah.
哦，没错。

27
00:01:06.650 --> 00:01:10.830
And this was actually Ken's sixth episode that he directed.
这其实是肯执导的第六集。

28
00:01:10.970 --> 00:01:12.290
We love Ken so much.
我们非常喜欢肯。

29
00:01:12.410 --> 00:01:21.570
I want you guys to know, if you watch the bloopers, you will see a few times Jen and Ken cracking up and they whip the camera over on them and bust them.
我想让你们知道，如果你看花絮，你会看到几次简和肯笑场，然后摄像机迅速转向他们，抓个正着。

30
00:01:21.690 --> 00:01:24.070
But they were just so fun on set, weren't they, Jenna?
但他们在片场真的很有趣，不是吗，珍娜？

31
00:01:24.230 --> 00:01:28.130
They were so, like, light and there for you and ready to laugh.
他们非常轻松，总是支持你，随时准备大笑。

32
00:01:28.130 --> 00:01:29.870
I loved the two of them together.
我喜欢他们俩在一起的感觉。

33
00:01:30.210 --> 00:01:30.450
Same.
我也是。

34
00:01:30.450 --> 00:01:32.970
All right, lady, should I hit you up with a summary?
好了，女士，我来给你做个总结好吗？

35
00:01:33.290 --> 00:01:35.790
Well, yeah, we got a lot to cover, so let's go.
好啊，我们要讲的内容很多，开始吧。

36
00:01:35.990 --> 00:01:38.050
Well, here's what we're going to talk about this week.
好吧，这就是我们这周要讨论的内容。

37
00:01:38.370 --> 00:01:47.910
On the day of the Dunder Mifflin Infinity website launch, Dwight makes it his goal to beat the website in sales to impress Angela.
在邓德·米夫林无限网站发布当天，德怀特的目标是销售额超过网站，以给安吉拉留下深刻印象。

38
00:01:48.610 --> 00:01:52.910
Jim and Pam pranked Dwight into thinking the computer is communicating with him.
吉姆和帕姆恶作剧骗德怀特说电脑在和他交流。

39
00:01:53.150 --> 00:02:04.610
And Michael thinks he got invited to the fancy launch party with sushi in New York, but he is embarrassed to learn he was only invited to attend virtually.
迈克尔以为自己受邀参加在纽约举办的寿司发布派对，但当他得知自己只是受邀参加虚拟会议时，感到非常尴尬。

40
00:02:04.610 --> 00:02:12.190
Yeah, he was invited to a chat room, which he thought was a club that had a secret password.
没错，他被邀请进了一个聊天室，他以为那是一个有秘密密码的俱乐部。

41
00:02:13.790 --> 00:02:14.430
Exactly.
没错。

42
00:02:14.910 --> 00:02:16.470
The password is password.
密码就是“密码”。

43
00:02:16.990 --> 00:02:17.230
Yeah.
是啊。

44
00:02:17.630 --> 00:02:21.010
Is there a WWW before that club name?
那个俱乐部名字前面有WWW吗？

45
00:02:22.330 --> 00:02:29.230
Well, listen, this episode also features a very famous cold open from the series.
听着，这一集还有该剧非常著名的开场片段。

46
00:02:29.530 --> 00:02:31.410
You know the one I'm talking about, Angela.
你知道我在说哪一个，安吉拉。

47
00:02:31.670 --> 00:02:32.190
I do.
我知道。

48
00:02:32.390 --> 00:02:32.950
I love it.
我喜欢那个片段。

49
00:02:33.090 --> 00:02:37.990
And Jenna, I have had people write in and tell me that they do this in their office now.
而且珍娜，有人写信告诉我，他们现在在办公室里也会这样做。

50
00:02:38.250 --> 00:02:38.670
Yes.
是的。

51
00:02:38.790 --> 00:02:40.270
That it sort of started a thing.
这算是开启了一个先例。

52
00:02:40.270 --> 00:02:44.370
When I watched this episode with Lee, he said, I've done this.
当我和李一起看这一集时，他说，我经历过这个。

53
00:02:44.490 --> 00:02:45.330
I've done this.
我经历过这个。

54
00:02:46.470 --> 00:02:59.050
So it's the one that takes place in the conference room and everyone's watching this little DVD square on the screen behind Michael as he is trying to lecture us about,
所以这一幕发生在会议室里，大家都在盯着迈克尔身后屏幕上的那个小DVD方块，当时他正试图给我们讲授……

55
00:02:59.350 --> 00:03:01.610
I don't know what, ideas to improve?
我不知道是什么，改进方案？

56
00:03:01.870 --> 00:03:02.050
Quarterly.
季度报告。

57
00:03:02.270 --> 00:03:02.610
Yeah.
没错。

58
00:03:02.810 --> 00:03:06.650
He's trying to tell us how to improve or spruce up the quarterlies, right?
他正试图告诉我们如何改进或润色季度报告，对吧？

59
00:03:06.790 --> 00:03:07.490
They're boring.
它们太无聊了。

60
00:03:07.830 --> 00:03:08.750
Very boring.
非常无聊。

61
00:03:09.810 --> 00:03:16.150
Well, we thought that today, in lieu of fast facts, we should do a deep dive on this cold open.
嗯，我们觉得今天与其讲快讯，不如深入剖析一下这个开场戏。

62
00:03:16.610 --> 00:03:20.270
We should, you guys, because there's some fun, fun info for you.
我们应该这么做，伙计们，因为这里面有一些非常有趣的资讯。

63
00:03:20.410 --> 00:03:25.910
So we reached out to our writer, Jen Salata, because we heard a rumor that this might have happened to her in her real life.
所以我们联系了我们的编剧简·萨拉塔，因为我们听说这可能在她的现实生活中发生过。

64
00:03:25.990 --> 00:03:27.610
It was somehow based on her, right, Jenna?
这在某种程度上是以她为原型的，对吧，珍娜？

65
00:03:27.890 --> 00:03:28.210
Yes.
是的。

66
00:03:28.390 --> 00:03:30.290
And she had some great stuff to say.
她分享了一些很棒的内容。

67
00:03:30.310 --> 00:03:32.750
So let's do a deep dive of this cold open.
那么，让我们深入剖析一下这个开场戏吧。

68
00:03:32.950 --> 00:03:34.670
Cold open deep dive, Sam.
开场戏深度剖析，萨姆。

69
00:03:34.910 --> 00:03:36.950
Will you play my son's sting?
能播放我儿子的转场音效吗？

70
00:03:36.950 --> 00:03:38.910
You got a deep, you got a dive.
你有深度，你有剖析。

71
00:03:39.130 --> 00:03:41.250
You put them together, get a deep dive.
把它们合在一起，就是深度剖析。

72
00:03:43.030 --> 00:03:43.910
There it is.
就是这个。

73
00:03:44.510 --> 00:03:45.730
There it is.
就是这个。

74
00:03:45.930 --> 00:03:46.410
All right.
好的。

75
00:03:46.530 --> 00:03:50.890
So like we said, Michael's having a meeting and behind him is this TV screen.
正如我们所说，迈克尔正在开会，他身后是那个电视屏幕。

76
00:03:50.890 --> 00:03:58.230
And you don't really know what's going on at first because it just keeps panning around to everyone in the conference room.
起初你并不知道发生了什么，因为镜头一直在会议室里的每个人身上扫来扫去。

77
00:03:58.230 --> 00:04:01.930
And we are oddly riveted by what Michael is saying.
而我们竟然被迈克尔所说的话深深吸引了。

78
00:04:02.510 --> 00:04:02.670
Yeah.
是啊。

79
00:04:02.830 --> 00:04:04.410
And what he's saying is so boring.
但他说的内容实在太无聊了。

80
00:04:04.570 --> 00:04:08.630
Like he's saying, I want to make suggestions to spruce up these quarterly reports.
比如他说，我想提议润色一下这些季度报告。

81
00:04:08.810 --> 00:04:17.250
He's saying things like, what if in a bad quarter there's a storm cloud or in a good quarter there's fireworks or a race car?
他说了一些诸如，如果季度表现不好，能不能加个乌云图标，或者表现好的话，加个烟花或赛车图标之类的建议？

82
00:04:17.250 --> 00:04:20.850
And then we all go, oh, and he goes, not a race car.
然后我们都说，哦，接着他说，不要赛车。

83
00:04:20.990 --> 00:04:22.150
It doesn't have to be a race car.
不一定要是赛车。

84
00:04:22.310 --> 00:04:25.630
So then we go to this gym talking head and he explains what's going on.
然后镜头转到吉姆的单人访谈，他解释了发生了什么。

85
00:04:25.850 --> 00:04:34.190
He says that they are all wanting to see if this little DVD cube on the TV screen will hit perfectly in the corner.
他说大家都在看电视屏幕上的那个DVD小方块会不会刚好撞进角落里。

86
00:04:34.190 --> 00:04:41.950
And he says he doesn't think it can happen and that Pam claims she saw it once when she was alone in the conference room.
他说他不认为这会发生，还说帕姆声称她有一次独自在会议室时看到过。

87
00:04:42.270 --> 00:04:44.470
And then, Jenna, it cuts to your talking head.
然后，珍娜，镜头切到了你的单人访谈。

88
00:04:44.590 --> 00:04:45.590
And you're so cute in this.
你在这一幕里太可爱了。

89
00:04:45.690 --> 00:04:47.270
You're like, I did see it.
你说，我确实看到了。

90
00:04:47.430 --> 00:04:48.490
Did Jim say I didn't see it?
吉姆说我没看到吗？

91
00:04:48.590 --> 00:04:49.430
It's very cute.
非常可爱。

92
00:04:49.670 --> 00:04:52.490
It seems like we get to see a little joke between Jim and Pam.
看起来我们看到了吉姆和帕姆之间的一个小玩笑。

93
00:04:53.130 --> 00:04:53.370
Yes.
是的。

94
00:04:53.550 --> 00:04:55.250
So then the boring meeting continues.
然后无聊的会议继续进行。

95
00:04:55.710 --> 00:04:57.810
And then finally it happens.
最后，那一刻终于发生了。

96
00:04:58.090 --> 00:05:01.050
The little cube goes in the square and everybody cheers.
小方块撞进了角落，大家都欢呼起来。

97
00:05:01.050 --> 00:05:04.510
And Michael thinks that it is because he has said something brilliant.
而迈克尔以为大家是因为他说了什么高明的话才欢呼的。

98
00:05:04.950 --> 00:05:05.070
Yeah.
是啊。

99
00:05:05.170 --> 00:05:07.590
His whole Where's Waldo thing was a big hit.
他那套“威利在哪里”的理论大获成功。

100
00:05:08.010 --> 00:05:09.610
And he's so happy.
他高兴坏了。

101
00:05:09.750 --> 00:05:11.790
Michael is like, hey, some days you just got it.
迈克尔就像是说，嘿，有时候你就是状态神勇。

102
00:05:12.070 --> 00:05:12.390
Yeah.
是啊。

103
00:05:12.510 --> 00:05:13.910
Some days you're just on fire.
有时候你就是势不可挡。

104
00:05:14.370 --> 00:05:14.690
Yeah.
没错。

105
00:05:14.930 --> 00:05:16.570
Well, I remember shooting this, Angela.
嗯，安吉拉，我记得拍这一幕的时候。

106
00:05:16.690 --> 00:05:17.670
It was so much fun.
真的特别好玩。

107
00:05:17.810 --> 00:05:20.530
But it was also like something we had to choreograph.
但它也像是一段我们需要编排的舞蹈。

108
00:05:20.690 --> 00:05:21.170
Do you remember?
你还记得吗？

109
00:05:21.470 --> 00:05:22.030
I do.
我记得。

110
00:05:22.610 --> 00:05:30.770
And guys, it is true that this cold open was based on a real life experience of Jen Salata in the writer's room.
伙计们，这个开场戏确实是基于编剧室里简·萨拉塔的真实经历。

111
00:05:31.050 --> 00:05:34.950
And it was the inspiration for her writing this little cold open.
这就是她写出这个小开场戏的灵感来源。

112
00:05:35.250 --> 00:05:36.710
We asked her about it.
我们问过她这件事。

113
00:05:36.830 --> 00:05:38.190
And here's what she had to say.
以下是她的讲述。

114
00:05:38.550 --> 00:05:48.490
So the inspiration for the cold open where the DVD logo bounces around the TV screen and everybody's transfixed was definitely the writer's room.
所以，DVD标志在电视屏幕上弹来弹去，大家看得目不转睛的开场戏，灵感绝对来自编剧室。

115
00:05:48.630 --> 00:05:50.230
I was obsessed with it.
我当时对此非常着迷。

116
00:05:50.350 --> 00:05:52.590
We would all watch the little DVD logo.
我们大家都会盯着那个小小的DVD标志看。

117
00:05:52.590 --> 00:06:02.950
And I remember that I saw it once hit perfectly in the corner, that the edge of the logo lined up with the edge of the TV, and it just felt so good.
我记得有一次我看到它完美地撞进了角落，标志的边缘和电视的边缘完全对齐了，那种感觉真是太爽了。

118
00:06:02.950 --> 00:06:13.570
And I remember there was at least one nonbeliever in the room, and it would hit like kind of close to the corner, and they'd say, that was it.
我记得当时屋里至少有一个人不信，标志撞得离角落有点近时，他们就会说，就是那个了。

119
00:06:13.610 --> 00:06:14.710
That must be what you remember.
你记得的肯定是那个。

120
00:06:14.710 --> 00:06:16.810
It's not going to hit perfectly in the corner.
它不可能完美地撞进角落的。

121
00:06:17.310 --> 00:06:26.990
And so I was transfixed with the logo and watching it a lot of the time and maybe not paying attention as much as I should have to the task at hand.
所以我当时被那个标志迷住了，大部分时间都在盯着它看，可能没怎么专心处理手头的工作。

122
00:06:26.990 --> 00:06:31.130
And so that is where the inspiration for it came from.
这就是灵感的来源。

123
00:06:32.370 --> 00:06:34.690
So basically, Jen was Pam.
所以基本上，简就是帕姆。

124
00:06:35.330 --> 00:06:43.590
Yes, Jen was Pam, and no one believed her, and she was adamant about it, and she wanted everyone else to see it go in the corner to, like, affirm her.
没错，简就是帕姆，没人相信她，但她非常坚持，她想让其他人也看到它撞进角落，以此来证明她是对的。

125
00:06:44.430 --> 00:06:45.930
This is what I love about Jen.
这就是我喜欢简的地方。

126
00:06:45.930 --> 00:06:48.310
If you guys have noticed, you've been listening to our podcaSt.
如果你们注意到了的话，你们一直在听我们的播客。

127
00:06:48.570 --> 00:06:51.770
Her episodes are so personal to her life experience.
她写的剧集都非常贴合她的人生经历。

128
00:06:51.770 --> 00:07:02.370
Yeah, I mean, the WebMD thing, remember, that she wrote about, and now this, and there's always these little moments from Jen's actual life, and I think it is such a nice touch.
是啊，我是说，还记得她写的关于WebMD的那集吗，现在又是这个，简的生活中总是有这些小瞬间，我觉得这真是个很棒的细节。

129
00:07:02.610 --> 00:07:11.490
And there are always these really ordinary moments that might otherwise pass you by, and something in her brain makes note of these.
总有一些非常平凡的时刻，本来可能会被你忽略，但她大脑里的某个部分会把它们记录下来。

130
00:07:11.910 --> 00:07:16.410
And that is why when you watch this cold open, it is so deeply relatable.
这就是为什么当你看到这个开场戏时，会觉得如此感同身受。

131
00:07:16.810 --> 00:07:18.050
It really is.
确实如此。

132
00:07:18.050 --> 00:07:19.970
I mean, Jenna, you and I both tempt.
我是说，珍娜，你和我都有过临时工经历。

133
00:07:20.170 --> 00:07:23.450
We sat through boring meetings all the time, and Jenna, you do this.
我们总是坐在无聊的会议里，珍娜，你就会这样做。

134
00:07:23.630 --> 00:07:32.010
You find little hooks of something happening to get you through it, and it's like sometimes nothing you even, like, speak about with your other coworkers.
你会找到一些小乐子来熬过会议，有时候甚至不需要和其他同事交流。

135
00:07:32.150 --> 00:07:35.050
You just all, like, lock onto something.
你们只是不约而同地锁定了某个东西。

136
00:07:35.490 --> 00:07:47.370
I tempt at this office, and all the executive side of the building faced, like, a nice view of the city, but everyone in cubicles faced a parking garage.
我在那家办公室做临时工时，大楼里行政区那边能看到不错的城市景观，但所有在隔间里的人面对的都是停车场。

137
00:07:47.370 --> 00:07:48.070
Okay.
好吧。

138
00:07:48.830 --> 00:07:49.270
Okay.
好吧。

139
00:07:49.470 --> 00:07:52.370
This parking garage became our entertainment.
这个停车场成了我们的娱乐来源。

140
00:07:52.890 --> 00:07:55.450
Like, every day, I'd be like, what's happening in the parking garage?
比如，每天我都会想，停车场里发生了什么？

141
00:07:55.770 --> 00:07:58.190
And they'd be like, oh, you remember Blue Zippy Guy?
